x676c: observe framebuffer content and display state during a bounded diagnostic boot

Opt-in sweetfb_trace records source/panel hashes, RGB565 thumbnails and calls
to unimplemented Mali/Scaler methods. DSI programming and stub return values
are unchanged. sweetakslog=0 suppresses successful AKS tracing, not failures.
sweetreboot=N syncs and invokes PSCI SYSTEM_RESET after N seconds; absent by
default. The timed kernel reset path still requires hardware validation.

